[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Variation "Advance Variation, Tal Variation"]
[ECO "B12"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "h-pawn-fight,solid-centre"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. h4 { White threatens h5, then g4 to chase the bishop. } 4... h5 { Stops White's pawn from reaching h5, which would take the g6 retreat square away from the bishop. }
5. c4 ( 5. Bd3 Bxd3 6. Qxd3 e6 7. Bg5 Be7 ) ( 5. Nc3 e6 6. Bd3 Bxd3 7. Qxd3 Qb6 )
5... e6 { Supports d5 against the c4 pawn and opens a square for the king's knight. }
6. Nc3 Ne7 { Heads for f5 or g6 and adds a second defender to d5. }
7. Nge2 Nd7 { Brings the last knight out and clears the way for ...dxc4 or ...c5 later. }
8. cxd5 ( 8. Ng3 Bg6 9. cxd5 cxd5 ) 8... cxd5 { Keeps a pawn on d5 that is hard to attack, and opens the c-file for Black's rook. }
9. Ng3 Bg6 { The bishop keeps its diagonal, and the pawn on h5 means it can no longer be chased. If White leaves the book, castle short, play ...Be7 and use the c-file. }
*
